          "recap_en": "According to a May 2026 BofA report, lower-income households saw after-tax wage growth of just 1.5% year-over-year in April, barely enough to cover rising gas costs, while higher-income households enjoyed 6.0% wage growth—offsetting gas spending nearly seventeen-fold. This \"K-shaped\" recovery has created the widest wage growth gap since 2015, with discretionary spending slowing for lower- and middle-income groups since gas prices began rising in March. For investors, this divergence signals potential headwinds for consumer-facing companies reliant on lower-income spending, while premium and luxury segments may remain more resilient.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美国银行2026年5月18日发布的报告，低收入家庭税后工资增速仅为1.5%（同比），几乎只能勉强覆盖汽油支出增长，而高收入家庭工资增速达6.0%，其工资增长可抵消汽油支出增幅的近17倍，两者差距创2015年以来最大。这一“K型”工资增长导致中低收入家庭自3月汽油价格上涨以来 discretionary spending（可自由支配支出）增速明显放缓。投资者应关注低收入群体消费能力承压对可选消费板块的潜在拖累，以及通胀环境下消费分化加剧的市场影响。",
