          "recap_en": "According to a May 2026 Bank of America Institute report, the pay premium for switching jobs has fallen to its lowest point in seven years, with job switchers seeing only an 8% year-over-year after-tax wage increase in Q1 2026, compared to 18% during the 2022 \"Great Resignation.\" While job switching ticked up to 13.5% in Q1 2026 from 12.9% a year earlier, it remains below pre-pandemic levels, and the narrowing gap between switchers (8%) and stayers (5%) suggests the labor market is cooling. For investors, this signals easing wage inflation pressure, which could support a less aggressive Federal Reserve stance but also indicates diminishing worker bargaining power.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美国银行研究所2026年5月21日发布的报告，跳槽带来的薪资溢价已降至七年来最低点：2026年第一季度，跳槽者税后工资同比增长8%，而留任者增长5%，两者差距远低于2022年“大辞职潮”时期的18%对7%。尽管跳槽率从2025年第一季度的12.9%微升至2026年同期的13.5%，但仍低于疫情前水平。这一趋势表明劳动力市场流动性减弱，投资者应关注企业用工成本趋稳对利润率的潜在支撑，以及消费支出增速可能放缓的风险。",
