          "recap_en": "**Recap:** BofA’s 2026 Summer Travel Outlook shows 77% of Americans plan to travel, led by Gen Z (93%), with a strong shift toward international destinations—Europe rising to 24% from 14% in 2025. Despite higher gas prices, most travelers are adjusting rather than canceling, though a K-shaped recovery is emerging: lower-income households are pulling back, while higher-income travel spending remains resilient. For investors, this signals continued strength in travel and entertainment stocks, but with a clear value-seeking consumer favoring rewards programs, AI trip planning (55% usage), and budget-conscious splurges on dining and experiences.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美银2026年夏季旅行与娱乐展望调查，77%的美国人计划出游，创历史新高，其中Z世代以93%的出行意愿领跑，且更倾向于为音乐会（32%）和体育赛事（20%）等体验消费。尽管高油价导致23%的人减少旅行次数，但55%的消费者仍优先追求高性价比体验，46%计划使用信用卡奖励等金融产品来抵消成本。对投资者而言，Z世代驱动的体验式消费、AI旅行规划工具（55%使用率）以及国际旅行需求回升（欧洲目的地同比增长10个百分点）值得关注，而低端消费疲软则提示经济分化风险。",
