          "recap_en": "According to BofA’s May Small Business Checkpoint, small business payroll growth continued to slow in April 2026, signaling a loss of momentum in the labor market, though transportation and healthcare remained positive contributors—particularly couriers and messengers. The data shows that rising operating costs, especially fuel, are making small firms hesitant to hire broadly. For investors, this suggests persistent margin pressure on small-cap and consumer-facing companies, while demand for last-mile delivery and healthcare services may offer relative resilience.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美国银行2026年5月19日发布的报告，4月美国小企业薪资增长持续放缓，但农业、零售、医疗和运输行业仍录得正增长，其中运输业因快递和信使服务需求强劲表现突出。数据显示，小企业整体薪资同比增速的三个月移动平均贡献中，运输业成为主要推动力，而医疗行业已连续一年多稳定支撑就业。这一趋势表明，尽管部分行业仍有韧性，但受燃料等运营成本上升影响，小企业招聘意愿可能继续承压，对劳动力市场构成潜在下行风险。",
