          "recap_en": "Despite massive AI capital expenditures—expected to total around $725 billion this year from Meta, Microsoft, Google, and Amazon—growth is increasingly driven by higher component prices, especially for memory, rather than actual deployment of more equipment. This pricing pressure, highlighted by Microsoft’s $25 billion cost increase and a projected slowdown in capex growth to just 10% next year, could eventually hurt Nvidia and its suppliers if the build-out pace slows in real terms. Investors should watch Nvidia’s earnings closely for signs of margin erosion, as the current boom may be masking a deceleration in volume-driven demand.",
          "recap_zh": "根据《华尔街日报》分析，尽管Meta、微软、谷歌和亚马逊今年资本支出预计高达约7250亿美元，但AI基础设施投资的增长主要源于芯片和内存等组件价格上涨，而非实际部署量的增加。例如，微软将190亿美元资本支出中的250亿归因于组件涨价，而英伟达虽预计本财季销售额达790亿美元（同比增长79%），但若成本推动型支出持续，可能抑制其芯片销量增长。投资者需警惕，若2027年支出增长放缓至10%且主要由通胀驱动，AI建设热潮的实际增速将低于表面数据，最终影响英伟达等供应商的长期盈利前景。"
