          "recap_en": "Based on Bank of America card data from January to April 2026, pet spending is heavily concentrated in the Western U.S., with Seattle leading at nearly 23% above the national average. In contrast, spending trails in Southern cities like Atlanta, Dallas, and Orlando, likely due to a lower cost of living. For investors, this highlights regional divergence in consumer discretionary spending on pet care, suggesting premium pet services and insurance may have stronger growth potential in higher-cost Western markets.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美国银行2026年5月发布的报告，基于2026年1至4月的信用卡消费数据，美国西部地区的宠物相关支出显著高于全国平均水平，其中西雅图的月均宠物消费（含宠物店、兽医和保险）比全国均值高出近23%；而亚特兰大、达拉斯和奥兰多等南部城市因生活成本较低，宠物支出低于全国水平。这一数据表明，区域性消费差异可能影响宠物行业相关公司的市场策略，投资者可关注西部城市宠物服务与保险业务的增长潜力。",
