          "recap_en": "According to BofA card data from early 2026, pet spending is heavily concentrated in the West, with Seattle leading at nearly 23% above the U.S. average, while Southern metros like Atlanta, Dallas, and Orlando trail below the national norm due to lower costs of living. The data highlights a clear regional divergence in pet-related expenditures, suggesting that companies in the pet care and insurance space may see stronger demand in higher-cost Western markets. For investors, this implies that regional exposure and cost-of-living dynamics are key factors when evaluating pet industry growth potential.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美国银行2026年1月至4月的信用卡消费数据，美国西部地区的宠物相关支出显著高于全国平均水平，其中西雅图的月均宠物消费比全国均值高出近23%，而亚特兰大、达拉斯和奥兰多等南部城市则因生活成本较低而低于全国水平。这一趋势表明，地域性消费差异在宠物经济中尤为突出，投资者可关注西部宠物零售、保险及兽医服务领域的增长机会。",
