          "recap_en": "Goldman Sachs argues that bond yields could keep rising, driven by a multi-year AI memory super cycle that will sustain semiconductor pricing power for three to five years, far longer than markets expect. Key data points include a projected 24x increase in token demand by 2030, China’s A-shares outperforming with a 10% year-to-date gain versus a 2% decline in the MSCI China index, and Japan’s bull case supported by political stability and corporate reforms. For investors, this suggests overweighting AI-related memory plays like South Korean semiconductor stocks, favoring onshore Chinese equities over offshore internet names, and maintaining exposure to Japan amid favorable macro and governance trends.",
          "recap_zh": "高盛指出，受AI记忆超级周期驱动，半导体存储芯片繁荣期将长达3-5年，远超市场预期，其中代币需求到2030年预计增长24倍，供应限制将维持定价权；同时，中国A股因政策支持和强劲盈利年内上涨近10%，而MSCI中国指数因互联网成分股盈利疲软下跌2%。日本股市在政治稳定、盈利增长和利率正常化等因素下保持吸引力。投资影响方面，水基础设施领域的公私合作模式及金融创新（如微融资和代币化融资）正为相关技术（如海水淡化和泄漏监测）带来规模化机会。"
