          "recap_en": "According to BofA Global Research, AI is more likely to augment jobs than replace them, with 13% of global employment showing augmentation potential versus only 2.3% at risk of automation, based on ILO data from 59 countries. The firm expects a two-stage adoption path similar to electrification, where AI first bolsters existing tasks before enabling broader occupational redesign. For investors, this suggests a focus on adaptability and task reallocation within companies rather than fearing mass job displacement.",
          "recap_zh": "根据美国银行2026年5月22日发布的报告，人工智能主要替代的是工作任务而非整个职业，国际劳工组织数据显示全球约13%的就业岗位具有“增强潜力”（即AI辅助人类），而仅有2.3%面临完全自动化风险。报告以电气化为例，指出突破性技术通常先融入现有流程，再逐步推动重组，预计生成式AI也将遵循类似的两阶段路径。这一发现意味着投资者应关注那些能够通过AI提升效率、而非简单替代人力的行业和公司，例如高收入国家中13.4%的岗位具备增强潜力，而自动化风险仅5.1%。",
