            {
              "en": "U.S. stocks climbed, bolstered by continued enthusiasm surrounding AI, aerospace and other emerging tech. The S&P 500 advanced 0.4%, the Dow gained 0.6%, and the Nasdaq edged up 0.2%. Indexes in Asia and Europe also climbed.\n\nKevin Warsh was sworn in as the nation’s top central banker. In remarks at today's swearing in ceremony, President Trump briefly endorsed Fed independence. But he quickly pivoted to arguments for why the Fed should view rising inflation as a one-off and keep rates lower to give the economy room to run.\n\nInvestors' optimism comes despite an uncertain backdrop surrounding the Middle East conflict, with media reports about a potential deal between the U.S. and Iran sending oil prices and government bonds swinging in recent days. Brent crude futures climbed 0.9% to $103.54 a barrel on Friday, while the 10-year Treasury yield edged lower to 4.57%.\n\nRepublicans are feeling the gloomiest they have felt about the economy since President Trump returned to the White House, according to the University of Michigan. Consumer sentiment among Republicans declined to 84.6 in May, the lowest reading of the current Trump administration, the school’s surveys of consumers showed Friday.",
              "zh": "美股上涨，受人工智能、航空航天及其他新兴科技领域持续热潮提振。标普500指数上涨0.4%，道琼斯指数上涨0.6%，纳斯达克指数微涨0.2%。亚洲和欧洲股指亦同步走高。\n\n凯文·沃什宣誓就任美国最高央行行长。在今日宣誓就职仪式上的讲话中，特朗普总统简短表态支持美联储独立性。但他随即话锋一转，阐述为何美联储应将当前通胀上升视为一次性现象，并维持较低利率以给经济留出运行空间。\n\n投资者的乐观情绪是在中东冲突带来的不确定背景下出现的，近日媒体关于美国与伊朗可能达成协议的报道导致油价和政府债券波动。周五布伦特原油期货上涨0.9%至每桶103.54美元，而10年期美国国债收益率小幅回落至4.57%。\n\n密歇根大学数据显示，共和党人对经济的悲观情绪达到特朗普总统重返白宫以来的最高水平。该大学周五公布的消费者调查显示，共和党人消费者信心指数5月降至84.6，为特朗普本届政府任期内最低值。"
