            },
            {
              "en": "Stocks rose amid signs that progress is being made to resolve the nearly three-month old war between the U.S. and Iran. The S&P 500 gained 0.2%, the Dow added 0.6%, and the Nasdaq advanced 0.1%. Brent crude fell.\n\nNvidia closed 1.8% lower. The chip giant reported record sales and income that beat analyst expectations, driven by demand for data-center computing and the rise of AI agents. But there's already a lot of optimism baked in. Nvidia’s stock is up 67% over the past 12 months, making it the largest publicly listed company in the world, with a market value of nearly $5.4 trillion.\n\nSpotify jumped 13%. The music streaming company said it plans to roll out an AI tool allowing users to make covers and remixes of songs from Universal Music Group artists.The company also gave a bullish 2030 outlook.\n\nWalmart said sales grew in its most recent quarter as shoppers looked for value and bought more online. Still, shares fell about 7% after the company left its financial expectations for the full year unchanged.\n\nSoftBank shares surged nearly 20% in Japan. OpenAI, one of its key investments, is preparing to file for an IPO as soon as this week.",
              "zh": "股市上涨，因有迹象显示，持续近三个月的美国与伊朗战争正取得解决进展。标普500指数上涨0.2%，道琼斯指数上涨0.6%，纳斯达克指数上涨0.1%。布伦特原油价格下跌。\n\n英伟达收盘下跌1.8%。这家芯片巨头公布的营收和利润均创纪录，超出分析师预期，主要受数据中心计算需求及人工智能代理崛起的推动。但市场已提前消化了大量乐观情绪。英伟达股价过去12个月累计上涨67%，使其成为全球市值最大的上市公司，市值接近5.4万亿美元。\n\nSpotify大涨13%。这家音乐流媒体公司表示，计划推出一款人工智能工具，允许用户对环球音乐集团旗下艺人的歌曲进行翻唱和混音。该公司还给出了看涨的2030年展望。\n\n沃尔玛表示，由于消费者追求性价比并增加线上购物，其最近一个季度的销售额实现增长。不过，该公司在维持全年财务预期不变后，股价下跌约7%。\n\n软银股价在日本飙升近20%。其重要投资对象之一OpenAI正准备最早于本周提交首次公开募股申请。"
            },
