            {
              "en": "Blame artificial intelligence. Excitement about the prospects for the new technology has encouraged companies to plow their profits back into capital spending rather than paying them out to shareholders, while boosting interest in stocks whose profits, and dividends, are merely hopes for the distant future.",
              "zh": "归咎于人工智能。对新科技前景的兴奋情绪，促使企业将利润重新投入资本支出，而非分配给股东，同时推高了那些利润与股息仅系于遥远未来的股票的热度。"
            },
            {
              "en": "The result has made the oldest way of picking dividend stocks—selecting steady payers that increase the “divi” every year—lag behind the index by the most over three years since the peak of the dot-com bubble in March 2000.",
              "zh": "这一结果使得最传统的股息股筛选方式——即选择那些每年稳定提高“股息”的股票——自2000年3月互联网泡沫顶峰以来的三年多时间里，跑输指数的幅度达到最大。"
            },
