          ],
          "recap_en": "Markets rallied on signs of U.S.-Iran de-escalation, with the S&P 500 up 0.2% and Brent crude falling, but Nvidia slipped 1.8% despite record sales and income, as its 67% annual gain and $5.4 trillion valuation suggest AI optimism is already priced in. Meanwhile, dividend investing is underperforming the S&P 500 by the most since the dot-com bubble, as AI-driven companies reinvest profits rather than pay dividends. Key movers included Spotify jumping 13% on an AI music tool and bullish 2030 outlook, Walmart falling 7% despite sales growth after keeping guidance unchanged, and SoftBank surging nearly 20% on OpenAI’s expected IPO filing.",
          "recap_zh": "今日美股上涨，标普500涨0.2%，纳斯达克涨0.1%，因美伊冲突有望缓解；但英伟达跌1.8%，尽管其数据中心和AI业务推动营收创纪录，股价过去12个月已涨67%，市值达5.4万亿美元。Spotify因计划推出AI音乐工具并给出乐观2030展望，股价大涨13%；沃尔玛季度销售增长但全年预期不变，股价下跌约7%。市场影响方面，AI热潮导致标普500股息收益率接近历史低点，传统股息策略表现落后于指数，投资者需关注科技股高估值与分红股之间的轮动风险。"
